{% from "components/lead-form.njk" import leadForm with context %}
{% import "components/blocks.njk" as b with context %}
{% set me = proof.team[0] %}

<section class="section section--soft">
  <div class="wrap--narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>I've spent my whole career fixing things that weren't working.</h1>
    <p class="lead mt-5">
      You're going to be dealing with one person, not a call center. So here's who that is.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{% if me and not me.placeholder %}
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap--narrow stack-lg">
    {% if me.photo %}
    <img src="{{ me.photo }}" alt="{{ me.name }}, {{ me.role }} at {{ site.name }}"
         width="320" height="320" class="team-photo" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    {% endif %}

    <p>
      I got into business at eighteen, running Smoothie King locations. For eleven years my
      job was to walk into a store that was losing money &mdash; sometimes four at once &mdash;
      put the right team in, cut what was bleeding, and rebuild it from the bottom up until it
      turned a profit and the people working there were glad to be there. Service with a smile,
      and actually meaning it.
    </p>
    <p>Same job now. The asset changed; the work didn't.</p>

    <h2>Where I am with this, honestly</h2>
    <p>
      I've been licensed since 2020 &mdash; six years as a broker, 40+ transactions listing,
      selling and renovating, and named Top Producer and #1 Rookie at my previous brokerage in
      2023 and 2024.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Most of that is agent-side. I'm building the buying side now, and I'd rather tell
      you that than pad a number.</strong> What you get from me is somebody who has been inside
      40+ of these transactions and knows exactly where they go wrong &mdash; and who will show
      you the arithmetic behind any offer I make, because I don't have a long buying record to
      hide behind yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've also done the unglamorous end of this. I've cut grass and mowed lawns to get
      somebody's house ready to show. I've looked after people's houses while they were out of
      town, because they trusted me with the keys. There isn't a part of this I think I'm
      above.
    </p>

    {#- All-or-nothing: this section reads as finished first-person copy, so it must not
        render its build-time placeholder to a visitor. No live review, no section. The
        placeholder still shows on /reviews/, where gaps are shown deliberately. -#}
    {% set liveAgentReviews = [] %}
    {% for r in proof.agentReviews.reviews %}
      {% if r.sourceUrl %}{% set liveAgentReviews = (liveAgentReviews.push(r), liveAgentReviews) %}{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% if liveAgentReviews.length %}
    <h3 class="mt-6">Somebody else's account of that, rather than mine</h3>
    <p>
      Here is the part I would rather you heard from a client than from me. Read the caveats
      first, because they matter: <strong>this is from my agent work, not a house we bought.
      It is from January 2023, and Thomasville is about ninety miles from here &mdash; Davidson
      County, not Gaston.</strong> It is not evidence that we have bought houses in your
      neighborhood, and I am not going to dress it up as though it were.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am showing it for one reason. This couple's house had been damaged by Hurricane Ian,
      they were still in Florida, and health problems made traveling to see houses genuinely
      hard. So I went and walked the houses for them. They bought one without ever standing in
      it, on my word about what I had seen.
    </p>
    {{ b.agentReviews() }}
    <p class="mt-5">
      If you are handling a property here from another state &mdash; an inherited house, a place
      you moved away from, a parent's home you are trying to sort out at a distance &mdash;
      that is the same job. You cannot get here, and you need somebody whose eyes you can
      trust when you are not in the room. That part transfers. The zip code does not, and I
      am not claiming it does.
    </p>
    {% endif %}

    <h2>Why Gaston and Cleveland County</h2>
    <p>
      We moved out here during the pandemic. We had kids, we were locked down in the city, and
      it was not the funnest experience. So we went to the country &mdash; space, a dog, room
      to spread out. Crowders Mountain, Kings Mountain National Military Park, Lake Wylie, Lake
      Norman. Local farms, the farmers market, little events for the kids. Less traffic, and
      people who'll actually talk to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've lived in North Carolina 23 years and worked all over the middle of it &mdash;
      Greensboro, High Point, Thomasville, Randleman, Asheboro, Salisbury, Kannapolis,
      Albemarle, Charlotte, Gastonia, Kings Mountain, Shelby. This is the part I chose to live
      in.
    </p>

    <h2>What I actually want out of a call</h2>
    <p>
      I want you to hang up better informed than you were, whether or not you ever sell me
      anything. If the answer is list it, I'll say list it. If the answer is call your servicer
      before you call anybody else, I'll say that. And if you go a different direction and it
      goes sideways six months later, call me anyway and ask what I'd do.
    </p>
    <p>What I'm after is being somebody you can lean on. That's the part of this I like.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--warm">
  <div class="wrap--narrow">
    <h2 class="mb-5">What I won't do</h2>
    <div class="promise">
      <ul class="promise__limits">
        <li><strong>Work with someone who lies about owning the property.</strong> If you're not
        on the deed and not willing to sign it, we're done.</li>
        <li><strong>Touch a house that's already been sold</strong> to somebody else.</li>
        <li><strong>Do business with somebody who shows up to the walkthrough drunk.</strong>
        Been there.</li>
        <li><strong>Chase you.</strong> If you've got a better offer, take it &mdash; just tell
        me, and tell me why, so I can get better at this. No hard feelings either way. Be
        straight with me and I'll be straight with you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="promise__closer">God first, then family, then business. That's the order, and it doesn't move.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
